    "notes": {
        "4ba38447-0549-4d6b-9bfa-314c34c99c19": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 560,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Trigger test assumptions\n\n- The trigger registers a Stripe webhook endpoint when the flow starts and deletes it when the flow stops. Stripe allows at most 16 endpoints per account: delete stale ones in the Dashboard (Developers → Webhooks) if the start fails.\n- **Keep the Wait 1m** before the provoking step so the endpoint is live.\n- The provoke creates a customer, a monthly price and a 14-day trial subscription; the trigger listens to Subscription Created only, so the cancel in the cleanup does not fire it again.\n- Use a test-mode secret key; other activity in the same account during the run can fire the trigger and fail the Assert."
        }
    }
